  "mic": "XTAL",
  "name": "Nasdaq Tallinn",
  "note": "2010-2024 sourced from exchange_calendars (backfill; not independently verified): 139 closures (138 named; exchange_calendars' one-off 2023-12-25 is Christmas Day and is named so) and no early closes, plus 9 corrections. exchange_calendars has no Christmas Day: it keeps Nasdaq Tallinn open on every weekday 25 December (only 2023 is closed, as an ad hoc day). Estonia's Public Holidays and Days of National Importance Act (in force since 23 February 1998; consolidated text https://www.riigiteataja.ee/public-api/api/v1/en/akt/527122022003/blob-html) lists 25 December, Christmas Day, as a public holiday and day of rest, and Nasdaq Tallinn's own investor calendar for week 52/2024 (https://view.news.eu.nasdaq.com/view?id=b8c140bf1e1581552fce9817b148ea449&lang=en) lists 24-26 December 2024 as trading holidays for TLN, RIG and VLN. So 25 December 2012, 2013, 2014, 2015, 2017, 2018, 2019, 2020 and 2024 are added as closures (2024 cites the exchange's notice, the rest the act) and are listed as contradicted_by on the 2010-2024 span: both libraries have them open. Ascension Day (not an Estonian public holiday) is a Nasdaq Baltic trading holiday: exchange_calendars closes it every year, and the exchange's investor calendar for week 19/2024 (https://view.news.eu.nasdaq.com/view?id=b81a517333cbff162b8fe11139cf51d93&lang=en) lists 9 May 2024 as a trading holiday for TLN, RIG and VLN; earlier years are not checked against the exchange. 2025-2026: exchange_calendars + exchange_publications. 2027-2029: standing pattern. Checked 2026-11-20 (4c10). Last published year: Nasdaq Baltic's trading-holiday calendar (https://nasdaqbaltic.com/statistics/en/calendar?holidays=1) lists for TLN in 2026: 1 January, 24 February, 3 and 6 April, 1 May, 14 May, 23 and 24 June, 20 August, 24, 25 and 31 December. The registry's 2026 weekday closures match exactly. No 2027 dates are posted yet, so 2027 joins the standing-pattern span. No shortened trading days are listed. Close (ADR 0013): Nasdaq Baltic's trading-day structure (https://nasdaqbaltic.com/market-information/trading-day/) gives Pre-Open 09:00-~10:00, continuous trading ~10:00-15:55, Pre-Close 15:55-~16:00, closing call 15:59:30-16:00:00 with the uncross at a random moment in that window, then Post-Trading to 16:30. ADR 0013 ignores the random window; the scheduled close is 16:00, unchanged (the file and exchange_calendars both have 16:00). One dated entry from 2010-01-01 (unconfirmed: the 16:00 end dates from 2 February 2009 per Nasdaq OMX's release of 19 November 2008, https://nasdaqbaltic.com/news/nasdaq-omx-baltic-market-to-extend-trading-hours/, but the closing-call structure in 2010 was not read). Post-trading is not modelled.",
